{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779228562,"nonce":"SfCzdeBmugV519itD98UtKEnHN8=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABCx0Hvg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/138","origin":"github"},"title":"mru_transform: choose durable nav-input source after 2026-05-19 ellipsoidal-vs-EKF discovery","message":"## Background\n\nDuring [#135 deployment (2026-05-19)](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/135) Phase 1, the nav stack failed to bring up mid-deployment:\n\n```\nlocal_costmap: Timed out waiting for transform from bizzy/base_link to bizzy/map_tide ... frame does not exist\nlifecycle_manager_navigation: Failed to bring up all requested nodes. Aborting bringup.\nbt_task_navigator: Action server is inactive. Rejecting the goal.\n```\n\n## Root cause (confirmed in-field — see gabby log §13)\n\n`sea_surface_estimator` was suppressing every tide estimate as implausible — observed estimate was ~`−12.8 m`, while the chart-datum plausibility band was `[−33.74, −19.42]`. With all estimates rejected, no `map → map_tide` transform was ever broadcast, cascading through `local_costmap` → `controller_server` → action-server activation failure.\n\nSnapshot of altitudes during the failure:\n\n| Source | Altitude | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/gps_pos` | +8.11 m (MSL) | with `undulation: -32.49 m`; ellipsoidal ≈ -24.38 m |\n| `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/ekf_nav` | +7.19 m (MSL) | with `undulation: -32.49 m`; ellipsoidal ≈ -25.30 m |\n| `/bizzy/mavros/global_position/global` | **-12.39 m** | (no undulation; EKF-fused) |\n| `/bizzy/tide_estimate` | **-12.44 m** | tracks mavros, not SBG |\n\n`/bizzy/tide_estimate` was tracking mavros `/global` (EKF-fused, referenced to EKF origin / home), **not** the ellipsoidal SBG MSL+undulation that the chart-datum band expects. Geoid undulation at this latitude is ~25 m; the mavros `/global` Z lands ~13 m above the plausible chart-datum band.\n\n## Triggering change\n\nCommit `e604a36e` (2026-04-28, `unh_echoboats_project11`) switched both `mru_transform` topic mappings in `config/bizzyboat.yaml` (lines 25 + 43):\n\n```diff\n-            position: \"mavros/global_position/raw/fix\"\n-            velocity: \"mavros/global_position/raw/gps_vel\"\n+            position: \"mavros/global_position/global\"\n+            velocity: \"mavros/local_position/velocity_body\"\n```\n\n`mavros/global_position/global` is ArduPilot's EKF-fused position; downstream `/bizzy/odom` therefore had a Z ~13 m above where chart-datum-aligned code expects the sea surface to be.\n\n## Field workaround (current state)\n\nField commit `c36acfa` (2026-05-19, on `gitcloud:field/unh_echoboats_project11` `jazzy`; cherry-picked onto PR #136 as `ece31dc`) reverted both lines back to `raw/fix` / `raw/gps_vel`. Mission completed on this workaround.\n\nPost-revert verification (gabby log §13):\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `bizzy/base_link` → `bizzy/map_tide` TF | ✓ resolved, Z = −0.078 m (boat 7.8 cm below sea surface — sane) |\n| `/bizzy/tide_estimate` | ✓ −23.77 m (inside plausible band) |\n| `sea_surface_estimator` suppression warnings (new log) | ✓ 0 |\n| Nav lifecycle (controller_server etc.) | ✓ all active |\n\n## Durable options\n\nThe revert is mission-enabling but not necessarily the right long-term choice. Three options to weigh:\n\n### A. Keep the revert: `mavros/global_position/raw/fix`\n\n- ✅ Restores pre-04-28 behavior; immediately works\n- ❌ Loses whatever the 04-28 switch was for (`raw/fix` may have less-clean velocity, no EKF benefits)\n- Cost: zero (already in place)\n\n### B. Switch to SBG: `sensors/sbg/gps_pos` (or `…/ekf_nav`)\n\n- ✅ Chart_datum is SBG-aligned (MLLW grids); puts the altitude in a coherent frame\n- ✅ Higher-quality nav data than raw GPS\n- ⚠️ **SBG is a temporary class-loaner** (returning after the June 2026 hydro class — see workspace memory `project_bizzyboat_sbg_temporary`). Hard-depending on `sbg_driver` is what that memory specifically warns against.\n- ❓ Needs message-type compat check (`mru_transform` expects what type?)\n- Cost: yaml swap + verification\n\n### C. Keep mavros `/global` with geoid compensation\n\n- ✅ Keeps EKF benefits\n- ✅ Doesn't depend on SBG\n- ❌ Most complex: need to compute ellipsoidal from EKF Z + known geoid undulation. EKF-origin / home semantics get involved.\n- Cost: real code change\n\n## Related work\n\n- `0507eda` (git-bug, no GitHub counterpart yet) — *nav: define lever-arm/base_link contract for SBG and mavros position streams*\n- `57a6134` (git-bug, no GitHub counterpart yet) — *urdf: model SBG INS, GNSS antenna(s), and IMU mounting alignment on bizzyboat*\n\nBoth are upstream of the nav-input choice — settling the lever-arm/base_link contract clarifies what frame each source actually publishes in. May be worth resolving those first.\n\n## Suggested next step\n\nDecide A vs B vs C with input from the upstream URDF/lever-arm work. Add a regression test on `sea_surface_estimator` plausibility-band agreement with the chosen source's altitude frame so this can't silently break again the next time a nav-input swap is considered.\n\nPart of #135\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}